{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTEpvc8CLr7HwVm5mfuk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, the processor may not send messages to the DLQ. **ADR 0024** (\"Keys that do not parse fail through redrive\", Accepted, 2026-10-20) covers this. Its agent rule is: \"Code never sends to the DLQ.\"\n\n- A key that doesn't parse fails like any other record. The processor doesn't delete the message, and after 5 receives the queue's redrive policy moves it to the DLQ.\n- This is a deliberate change from the design doc, which sends such messages straight to the DLQ. That would need `sqs:SendMessage` on the DLQ, and the processor's role doesn't have that permission.\n- ADR 0023 sets the local and test value of \"redrive after 5 receives\".\n\nFiles used:\n- `docs/architecture/decisions/0024-unparseable-keys-fail-through-redrive.md`\n- `processor/CLAUDE.md` (line 54: \"Never send to the DLQ… (ADR 0024)\")\n- `processor/ARCHITECTURE.md` (line 5)\n- `docs/architecture/decisions/0023-processor-config-defaults.md` (line 11)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":8060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"output_tokens":370,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"100b7837-8af6-48c8-8756-34b38cd069ea","uuid":"fb8aae9b-8408-4a75-af56-6eb93ee0041d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:46:42.702Z","request_id":"req_011CgTEpvHXVsqNUe7nX8BUu"}
